[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options / modes / flags:** none.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `lib.h` exposes exactly one entry point and it takes no flag, mode, enum, or
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m context argument:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void rgb_to_hsv(float *dest, const float *src);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no `#ifdef`s in `lib.c`, no global configuration state, no
