[38;5;252m[1m## What the library is[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc_src[0m is a single translation unit exporting one function: [38;5;10mvoid rgb_to_hsv(float *dest, const float *src)[0m. No flags, no enums, no length parameters, no error channel — so the whole surface is driven by input shape.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## One real divergence found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m diverged from the C on null pointers [1min the debug profile[22m: [38;5;10mrustc[0m instruments plain [38;5;10m*ptr[0m derefs when [38;5;10mdebug_assertions[0m are on, so the Rust library died with [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m and a panic message where the C died with [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m. The C has no null check, so this was a genuine behavioral difference visible to any consumer of the debug artifact.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fixed in the Rust (never the C) by doing the three loads and three stores with [38;5;10mread_volatile[0m/[38;5;10mwrite_volatile[0m, which rustc does not instrument. Both libraries now fault identically in every profile, and the C's "all reads before any write" ordering — which the aliasing rows depend on — is now explicit rather than left to the optimizer.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
